# DESIGN.md, Adaptive list-detail. `split`'s sibling for hosts that
# CANNOT resize: it never resizes and never names a presentation, so the
# BARE `expect_split` (a regular window must not show ONE pane while its
# stack holds two) is true at every width a lane can hand it — which is
# also why there is no `back`. Picking a device outside the 400..840
# band is the LANE's job. NO expect_title, deliberately: this and
# `split` are the SAME app, and one app has one title.
expect_entries 0
expect_split
click button#0
expect_entries 1
expect label#0 "list pane"
expect label#last "detail pane"
# With an entry on the stack, a regular window owes two panes.
expect_split
# The one assertion here that reads a REAL tree on every lane: `expect
# label#last` above reads kaya's model and passes for an arm that ran
# and drew nothing.
expect_ax label#last "label/detail pane"
